# Shell scripts run inside the Linux container (api/scripts/start.sh is the web dyno's command).
# Keep them LF even on Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true, or `sh` fails with
# "set: Illegal option -" when the image is built locally.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files: never convert line endings, on any machine. Without this, git guesses, and small
# PDFs with no NUL byte were treated as text: a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true added a
# \r to every line, so the sample PDFs on that machine no longer matched the ones Vercel serves,
# and the API's sample hashes (taken from that checkout) rejected every sample in production.
*.pdf binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
